{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1416375-anyone-converted-mage-wonders-and-talismans-to-exalted-s-artifacts","id":1416375,"title":"Anyone converted Mage Wonders and Talismans to Exalted's Artifacts?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-10-01T16:10:36-07:00","id":1416375,"title":"Anyone converted Mage Wonders and Talismans to Exalted's Artifacts?","content":"I've seen a wealth of awesome shit in Mage, some of it normal, and some of it homebrewed. Anyone has good ways or examples of conversion to Exalted?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-01T16:20:04-07:00","id":1416376,"title":"","content":"Can you be more specific in what you're looking for in terms of a &quot;conversion?&quot;<br /> <br /> Are we talking Mage to Exalted? If so... what specifically about Mage's methods do you feel are worth converting to Exalted?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-01T17:07:07-07:00","id":1416382,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1416375-anyone-converted-mage-wonders-and-talismans-to-exalted-s-artifacts?p=1416376#post1416376\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can you be more specific in what you're looking for in terms of a &quot;conversion?&quot;<br /> <br /> Are we talking Mage to Exalted? If so... what specifically about Mage's methods do you feel are worth converting to Exalted?</div> </div> </div> </div>Large numbers of Wonders and Talismans. For example, this: <br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://forums.sufficientvelocity.com/threads/white-wolfs-world-of-darkness.6205/page-527#post-8091046\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forums.sufficientvelocity.com/data/svg/20/1/1794123741/logo_icon.png\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://forums.sufficientvelocity.com/threads/white-wolfs-world-of-darkness.6205/page-527#post-8091046\" target=\"_blank\"> White Wolf's World of Darkness </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://forums.sufficientvelocity.com/threads/white-wolfs-world-of-darkness.6205/page-527#post-8091046\" target=\"_blank\"> https://forums.sufficientvelocity.com/threads/white-wolfs-world-of-darkness.6205/page-527#post-8091046 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> No. He took the flaw that makes everyone around him have his children with the slightest indirect physical contact, but he used those extra points to buy the merit that makes Garou have Delerium when they see his Archid form. \"Hey, you know how you guys murdered humans so hard for so long... </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> IX-5S Intelligent Personal Defense Weapon/IX-5S2 Advanced Intelligent Personal Defense Weapon (Wonder)<br /> Enlightenment 3 (6 Points) for the IX-5S, Enlightenment 4 (8 points) for the IX-5S2<br /> <br /> The IX-5S IPDW fires self-guiding micromunitions and provides a low skill, compact personal defense weapon for Technocratic agents. Because the IX-5S renders operator skill effectively irrelevant, many combat operatives who are tasked with escorting non-combat oriented Technocrats on a regular basis keep one handy-it's a weapon you can give to your charge for self-protection without the risk of them shooting you in the back. Similarly, Virtual Adepts and Etherites who have had the good luck to capture, bootleg, or otherwise acquire IX-5S platforms find them incredibly useful tools to give to people who can't shoot straight. In the hands of a dedicated combatant, the IX-5S is more useful for sweeping the field of multiple hostile targets at once than as a primary weapon for engagement of high-end enemy combatants (therefore, its &quot;personal defense weapon&quot; moniker).<br /> <br /> The IX-5S can be fired as a normal pistol, but it gains no special benefits from doing so. Instead, a character should take &quot;Aim&quot; actions with the weapon to lock it onto targets within the weapon's effective range. A Mind 2/Entropy 1 effect locks the weapon onto hostiles and also prevents it from locking onto friendlies. The firer may lock onto up to [Enlightenment] targets per Aim action. No target may be locked more than once. When the character fires, a Forces 2/Correspondence 1 effect guides individual rounds to different target. These attacks are all made in a single action, treated as if they had rolled 5 successes each, and ignore all modifiers for cover, poor lighting, operator distraction, or range. The IX-5S may attack as many targets in a single turn as it has ammunition. A character may not aim and fire the IPDW in the same turn without some source of extra actions (such as Time 3). Once fired at a locked target, all locks are expended and the weapon must be locked-on again.<br /> <br /> The upgraded IX-5S2 allows for up to 3 locks to be assigned to a single target and has higher Enlightenment. In all other aspects, it is equivalent to the IX-5S.<br /> <br /> Paradox flaws for the IPDW include lock-on system failures, IFF malfunctions, and the standard litany of weapon jams and malfunctions that can happen in the heat of combat. The IPDW is generally coincidental, because the operator's inexplicable accuracy is hard to notice and can be explained away as good marksmanship or just luck.<br /> <br /> IX-5S: Damage 6L, Rate 3 (manual)/12 (lock-on), Range 50, Magazine 12, Conceal J. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-01T18:14:53-07:00","id":1416396,"title":"","content":"OK...<br /> <br /> That seems a very problematic example for a few reasons:<br /> <br /> 1) Firearms are not a major part of Exalted. A firedust weapon that can fire multiple times before reloading is already an Artifact in Exalted, and that's still just a glorified burst of flame rather than firing potent munitions. The equivalent of a semi-automatic pistol that's not magical at all in Mage, is already a 3 or 4 dot Artifact in Exalted, and probably needs magic to make ammunition for.<br /> <br /> 2) Exalted's Artifacts are usually single function unless you're using 2e's magitech or 3e's Evocations. Both of those add additional complications that don't directly translate to more dots for the value of the item like Mage does.<br /> <br /> 3) This also very much ignores how much Exalted don't need magical items for this stuff. A dedicated ranged fighter in Exalted has Charms to cover lots of successes, attacking multiple targets per turn, and ignore penalties.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}